  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for node NRS_484B_213_2c on the second of the six allowed runs. All five witnesses gave their planned verdicts and the rule needs no other rule.\n\n**Gate runs**\n1. `CHECK_FAIL`, a unit mismatch. The \"moving toward the bridge\" test compared a dot product (velocity × distance, m²/s) with a zero in metres. I rewrote it as `vx·dx > −(vy·dy)`, which is the same condition with the same unit on both sides, so no new literal was needed.\n2. `OK`.\n\n**The rule**\n- **Who it covers:** members of `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** all three of these hold:\n  - the vehicle is not on a one-way roadway;\n  - the view is obstructed: the sight distance of a highway the vehicle occupies is below its speed × `p.passing_sight_time`;\n  - some bridge, viaduct or tunnel is within 100 ft of the vehicle's body, and the vehicle's velocity points toward it.\n- **The duty:** for every centre line lying on a highway the vehicle occupies, the vehicle's lateral offset to that line is not negative, so the vehicle is not left of it.\n\n**One choice the node left open (declared as a narrowing on s3):** the node says \"sight distance at the subject's point\" but doesn't say which region it is read from. I read it from the highway region the vehicle occupies. That is the only region type the node claims that contains the vehicle.\n\n**Witnesses:** a motor vehicle heads east at 20 m/s toward a bridge 7.5–17.5 m ahead. At that speed the sight-distance bound is 220 m.\n\n| Witness | Setup | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | left of the centre line, sight distance 100 m | violated |\n| permit | right of the centre line, sight distance 100 m | compliant |\n| idle | left of the centre line, sight distance 1000 m | not applicable |\n| blind | left of the centre line, sight distance not observed | unknown |\n| branch_1 | as forbid, on a one-way roadway | not applicable |\n\nFiles are in the working directory:\n- `task_result.md`\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_213_2c.lean` (rule)\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_213_2c.lean` (witnesses)",
